Objectives:
1. Prevent loss of additional vegetative cover;
2. Prevent loss of soil through erosion (wind and water) and on-site productivity of ecological sites;
3. Prevent the loss of water control and deterioration of water quality;
4. Prevent damage to property on and off-site;
5. Prevent the invasion of burned areas by highly flammable plants which produce a high potential for a reburn and additional site deterioration;
6. Prevent the loss of fish and wildlife habitat;
7. Provide available vegetation to sustain livestock active preference and wild horse management numbers.
